  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Arab-Israeli Conflict: Israel/Jordan Trust to Enhance Defense &amp; Security Cooperation Seminar 01-21</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this series seeks to build trust and strengthen cooperation between Israel and its Arab neighbors. The series will begin with a seminar on Israel and Jordan. Both have a stake in solving the Palestinian issue, curbing Iranian influence, countering extremist and radical forces, and achieving regional stability. Both are major non-NATO allies of the United States and cooperate with Washington on critical defense and intelligence issues. Jordan is the second Arab country after Egypt to sign a peace treaty with Israel, yet faces growing domestic pressure to terminate the treaty in the absence of a settlement with the Palestinian issue. This seminar seeks to explain and analyze these issues. By hearing different viewpoints, participants will have a firm basis to explore ways to advance cooperation and strengthen trust as a strategic national interest for all parties.</narrative>
  </description>
